				"paragraphStyle": {
					"__type": "textStyle"
				},
				"string": "# Catalyst Plugins\n\nCatalyst Plugins connect Catalyst to external systems, engines, tools, and services.\n\nA component is part of Catalyst. A plugin connects Catalyst to something outside Catalyst.\n"
			},
			{
				"__type": "textSnippet",
				"children": {
					"__type": "snippets",
					"items": []
				},
				"createEmail": {
					"__type": "email",
					"emailString": "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime": {
					"__type": "time",
					"time": {
						"__type": "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString": "2026-05-14T14:00:07.115881+10:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail": {
					"__type": "email",
					"emailString": "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime": {
					"__type": "time",
					"time": {
						"__type": "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString": "2026-05-14T14:00:07.115881+10:00"
					}
				},
				"uid": {
					"__type": "uid",
					"uidString": "Zz7AqQchSsms/xskfvNnPQ=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle": {
					"__type": "textStyle"
				},
				"string": "## Examples\n\n- Unreal Engine integration\n- Voxel Plugin Pro integration\n- external editor bridges\n- runtime presentation clients\n- third-party service integrations\n\nPlugin docs should explain the boundary clearly: what Catalyst owns, what the external system owns, and how data moves between them.\n"
			}
		]
